cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use xingo-sparse, please cite it using these metadata. The concept DOI below resolves to the latest version; each release has its own DOI on Zenodo."
type: software
title: "xingo-sparse: sparse linear algebra for optimization solvers"
abstract: "Sparse linear algebra for optimization in pure Rust: generic CSC/CSR containers, a threshold-pivoting LU for simplex bases with Forrest-Tomlin updates and hypersparse solves, AMD and COLAMD orderings, scaling, and regularized, refined KKT solvers for interior-point methods. The linear algebra layer of the Xingó solver."
authors:
  - family-names: Leite
    given-names: André
license: "MIT OR Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/StrategicProjects/xingo-sparse"
url: "https://strategicprojects.github.io/xingo-sparse/"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24095312
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-09
keywords:
  - sparse linear algebra
  - LU factorization
  - Forrest-Tomlin
  - AMD
  - COLAMD
  - KKT
  - interior-point method
  - simplex method
  - Rust
